  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1225 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nThe rest of the forecast for the rest of the week will be relatively \nbenign. The upper high will remain over the southeast CONUS through \nlate week. Upper ridging will stretch far enough westward to keep \nthe forecast dry with upper southwesterly monsoon flow staying well \nto our west. The plus side is temps should stay fairly steady and \nnot too hot through much of the week. The upper high is still \nprogged to retrograde over the weekend, eventually settling over the \ncentral CONUS. This would bring the return of more widespread 100 \ndegree highs while continuing dry conditions.",
